    "summary": "Model built and passed all L1/L2/L3 checks after one repair round.\n\nRoot cause of the initial failure: the instance stored girder section top-slab thickness t_top = 0.20 m, contradicting the description (\"top slab 0.18 m thick\") and the already-accepted section-property decisions (computed from 0.18 m). This created an L2-1 inconsistency (component parameters not reproducible from provenance decisions) and invalidated the dependent girder decisions. Fixed by rewriting the instance section with t_top = 0.18 m and re-proposing the withdrawn girder decisions (single A=1.0605 m², single I=0.25166 m⁴, A=5.30260 m², I=1.25829 m⁴, Ec=32500 MPa, γ=26.0 kN/m³, w=137.868 kN/m, m=14.0538 t/m). lane.mu had also been withdrawn and was re-decided.\n\nFinal model: single simply-supported span, 25 m bearing-to-bearing; 5 precast prestressed small-box girders (C40), small_box section h=1.4 m, b_top=2.4 m, b_bottom=1.0 m, t_top=t_bottom=0.18 m, t_web=0.20 m; two plain laminated elastomeric bearings (300×350 mm, 4×8 mm rubber layers) under each girder end → 10 per support line; spine-beam 2D idealization. Loads: self-weight of girders only plus Highway Class II (4 lanes, qk=7.875, Pk=232.5 kN, ξ=0.67).\n\nKey results: first vertical bending frequency f1 = 4.272 Hz; impact factor μ = 0.2409; total self-weight reactions 1723.3 kN per abutment (Σ = 3446.7 kN = γ·A·L ✓); self-weight midspan moment 10770.9 kN·m; lane-load max positive moment 6878.4 kN·m."
